WEBVTT

00:00:01.050 --> 00:00:02.760
<i>My name is Kakeru Aizawa.</i>

00:00:03.270 --> 00:00:05.800
<i>After miraculously surviving that accident,</i>

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:08.080
<i>I was unable to quit soccer</i>

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:09.530
<i>and had been living my life aimlessly.</i>

00:00:10.230 --> 00:00:14.530
<i>One day, I found out that 
my transplanted heart</i>

00:00:14.530 --> 00:00:15.860
<i>belonged to my brother.</i>

00:00:16.570 --> 00:00:20.410
<i>As the recipient of my brother, 
Suguru Aizawa's, last pass,</i>

00:00:20.410 --> 00:00:23.750
<i>I decided to continue playing 
soccer with my brother.</i>

00:00:24.080 --> 00:00:26.800
<i>I won't waver, I won't run away,</i>

00:00:26.800 --> 00:00:29.110
<i>as long as the life he gave me lasts.</i>

00:02:00.760 --> 00:02:06.060
<b>Enoshima High Football Club?!</b>

00:02:10.350 --> 00:02:11.800
What do you think, Brother?

00:02:12.610 --> 00:02:14.860
This is the Enoshima High uniform.

00:02:14.860 --> 00:02:16.530
Today's the inaugural ceremony.

00:02:16.530 --> 00:02:18.510
I'm attending with Kakeru.

00:02:18.510 --> 00:02:20.280
How do we look, Suguru-san?

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:22.480
Well, I'm heading out.

00:02:22.940 --> 00:02:23.960
I'll see you later.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.260
Inaugural Ceremony
Enoshima High School

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:50.870
You'll finally get to meet Araki-san.

00:02:51.260 --> 00:02:52.190
Yeah...

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.080
Real men play baseball!

00:02:52.190 --> 00:02:54.080
Are you interested in playing basketball?

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:52.690
Come!!   Recruiting!!   Tennis Club

00:02:52.690 --> 00:02:55.400
Karate Club   Recruiting

00:02:54.080 --> 00:02:55.230
We're the tennis club!

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:56.650
We're the badminton club!

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:56.650
Baseball Club

00:02:56.670 --> 00:03:00.610
Feel the Youth of Adolescence!   Now!
Join the Tennis Club!

00:02:56.930 --> 00:02:58.750
Clubs are so popular here.

00:02:58.750 --> 00:03:00.610
I know. It seems like so much fun!

00:03:01.400 --> 00:03:02.910
It'd be nice if there was

00:03:02.910 --> 00:03:04.540
a girl's soccer team, too.

00:03:04.540 --> 00:03:08.700
Then you would be the 
ace player, right away.

00:03:08.700 --> 00:03:10.210
For now, I'll be fine in

00:03:10.210 --> 00:03:12.540
the same soccer club as you, 
as a manager.

00:03:12.540 --> 00:03:14.210
Yes, yes, yes!

00:03:14.210 --> 00:03:18.380
I'll escort you two to the soccer club!

00:03:25.290 --> 00:03:27.560
They're in a really remote location.

00:03:27.900 --> 00:03:30.020
Ah, um... Senpai?

00:03:30.480 --> 00:03:31.220
Huh?

00:03:31.590 --> 00:03:33.290
I'm Makoto Hyodo.

00:03:33.290 --> 00:03:34.190
Call me Mako.

00:03:34.190 --> 00:03:36.780
Mako-san, I heard that there was

00:03:36.780 --> 00:03:39.580
a second year midfielder named 
Araki-san in the soccer club.

00:03:39.580 --> 00:03:41.400
Hmm? You know Araki?

00:03:41.400 --> 00:03:43.860
Well, at least that he 
has an amazing pass...

00:03:44.260 --> 00:03:47.830
His receivers have got it rough!

00:03:47.830 --> 00:03:50.090
I've been running combinations 
with him for a year now,

00:03:50.090 --> 00:03:52.830
but I never get a word in edgewise, 
what with his machine gun speed.

00:03:54.430 --> 00:03:57.700
So he does have quite 
a bit of momentum.

00:03:58.390 --> 00:04:01.330
Word in edgewise? Machine gun?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:06.430
Hey, you're cute.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:08.320
Have a flower.

00:04:08.320 --> 00:04:09.390
No, thanks.

00:04:12.560 --> 00:04:14.740
You wear soccer shoes all the time?

00:04:14.740 --> 00:04:16.480
And pretty nice ones, at that.

00:04:17.430 --> 00:04:19.760
I wear them all the time 
so they're broken in.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.900
I just change the studs for matches.

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.870
I like this kid. 
You're quite unique.

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.540
Um... Mako-senpai?

00:04:32.010 --> 00:04:33.830
Oh, sorry, sorry.

00:04:34.570 --> 00:04:37.140
Second years, Kurebayashi and Horikawa.

00:04:37.140 --> 00:04:39.290
What? Oh, n-nice to meet you.

00:04:39.290 --> 00:04:40.390
Coach!

00:04:39.320 --> 00:04:42.720
<b>Enoshima High FC</b>

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:42.720
I've brought along some 
freshmen hoping to join.

00:04:42.940 --> 00:04:44.600
Soccer quiz!

00:04:47.490 --> 00:04:50.360
If you get it right, 
you can join the club!

00:04:51.240 --> 00:04:52.860
Here is your question:

00:04:53.310 --> 00:04:56.600
What song do you sing on 
the field when it's raining?

00:04:58.110 --> 00:04:59.730
Hey, answer, newcomer.

00:04:59.730 --> 00:05:01.400
Uh, um...

00:05:02.650 --> 00:05:05.590
Oh! Pitch, pitch, chappu, chappu.

00:05:05.590 --> 00:05:07.200
Run, run, run!

00:05:07.200 --> 00:05:08.490
Correct!

00:05:09.230 --> 00:05:10.900
All right!

00:05:11.960 --> 00:05:14.710
Congratulations.
 I permit you to join the club.

00:05:14.710 --> 00:05:16.680
Write down your name, your class,

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:17.740
your cell phone number,
 and your email address.

00:05:17.740 --> 00:05:19.290
O-Okay.

00:05:21.150 --> 00:05:22.900
Was that all right?

00:05:22.900 --> 00:05:24.260
It was perfect.

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.100
We've got to recruit members 
by any means necessary.

00:05:32.640 --> 00:05:34.100
I'm by the window.

00:05:34.100 --> 00:05:35.560
And I'm one away.

00:05:42.800 --> 00:05:43.980
Keep it down.

00:05:43.980 --> 00:05:45.170
Kota-kun?

00:05:45.170 --> 00:05:46.840
What are you doing here?

00:05:46.840 --> 00:05:48.900
What am I doing here?
 I'm a student.

00:05:48.900 --> 00:05:49.700
You got a problem with that?

00:05:49.700 --> 00:05:51.810
Now that you mention it, 
I heard your grades weren't too good

00:05:49.720 --> 00:05:57.410
<b>Congratulations
This is 1-B \(^o^)/

00:05:51.810 --> 00:05:54.360
and you couldn't get into Kama High...

00:05:54.360 --> 00:05:57.410
Yeah, I panicked, but luckily 
on the second application—

00:05:57.410 --> 00:05:59.530
What am I telling you for?!

00:06:00.090 --> 00:06:02.090
All right, everyone take a seat.

00:06:03.110 --> 00:06:05.840
Everyone in 1-B, nice to meet you.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.430
I'll be your homeroom teacher.

00:06:08.430 --> 00:06:10.050
My name is Teppei Iwaki.

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.540
I'd like to start by explaining 
the schedule today.

00:06:10.990 --> 00:06:12.300
He was the one who...

00:06:12.300 --> 00:06:13.540
So he's our homeroom teacher.

00:06:13.540 --> 00:06:15.950
After this, we'll go to 
the inaugural ceremony,

00:06:13.930 --> 00:06:17.020
Quit whispering behind my back!

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:17.020
so once we go to the gym...

00:06:17.040 --> 00:06:19.520
Enoshima High School   26th Inaugural Ceremony

00:06:17.320 --> 00:06:19.000
...is what we believe.

00:06:19.520 --> 00:06:22.290
Therefore, we'd like to recommend

00:06:22.290 --> 00:06:25.540
that all incoming students explore 
the numerous clubs

00:06:25.540 --> 00:06:29.210
which fall under the governance of the school.

00:06:26.190 --> 00:06:27.860
<i>He's in here, isn't he?</i>

00:06:27.860 --> 00:06:29.990
<i>The midfielder my brother respected.</i>

00:06:29.990 --> 00:06:31.240
<i>Araki-senpai...</i>

00:06:32.310 --> 00:06:34.860
In other words, the body and the mind

00:06:32.350 --> 00:06:35.580
If they knew the truth, 
they'd quit, wouldn't they?

00:06:34.860 --> 00:06:37.650
are like the front and 
back tires of a car...

00:06:35.580 --> 00:06:37.690
We won't let them quit.

00:06:37.690 --> 00:06:40.510
No matter what, we're pulling 
that Aizawa guy in.

00:06:40.990 --> 00:06:43.930
We need every recruit we can get.

00:06:47.550 --> 00:06:50.550
Want to go see the soccer club?

00:06:50.550 --> 00:06:52.560
Yeah. I wonder if Araki-senpai 
will be there?

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:54.420
I've heard they're pretty good,

00:06:54.420 --> 00:06:57.020
but I'll become a regular, Nana-chan.

00:07:00.740 --> 00:07:03.670
That merciless comeback was great!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:07.500
I'm from the comic duo research club.

00:07:07.500 --> 00:07:09.440
I've been waiting for a newcomer

00:07:09.440 --> 00:07:12.300
who can throw comebacks like that.

00:07:12.300 --> 00:07:14.780
How about all of you join our club?

00:07:14.780 --> 00:07:16.850
I'm sorry.

00:07:16.850 --> 00:07:19.650
We've already decided 
on the soccer club.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:21.080
The soccer club?

00:07:21.080 --> 00:07:22.450
I wouldn't, if I were you.

00:07:22.450 --> 00:07:24.500
They're totally boring.

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:26.580
I'm not joining to be bored

00:07:26.580 --> 00:07:29.280
or to have fun, but to play soccer!

00:07:29.830 --> 00:07:31.310
Let's go, Kakeru.

00:07:33.370 --> 00:07:35.680
What was the deal with that fatty?

00:07:36.200 --> 00:07:39.640
...especially if you 
want to play soccer.

00:07:42.940 --> 00:07:44.000
Next!

00:07:47.500 --> 00:07:50.100
Looks like a passing drill where 
you have to avoid the cones.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:51.700
I wonder if they're all seniors...

00:07:53.910 --> 00:07:55.950
He's pretty good.

00:07:57.670 --> 00:08:00.720
Number 5, you fail. The test is over.

00:08:00.720 --> 00:08:01.330
What?

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:02.410
Test?

00:08:02.410 --> 00:08:04.830
This is the try-out test?

00:08:05.310 --> 00:08:08.680
B-But... when I went 
to write my name down,

00:08:08.680 --> 00:08:10.550
they all seemed to welcome me...

00:08:10.550 --> 00:08:13.120
Um, why? Did I do something...

00:08:13.510 --> 00:08:16.650
The coach told you to 
use an inside kick!

00:08:16.650 --> 00:08:17.510
But...

00:08:17.510 --> 00:08:18.500
Next!

00:08:19.210 --> 00:08:20.860
That's so strict!

00:08:20.860 --> 00:08:22.770
Boring, isn't it?

00:08:22.770 --> 00:08:23.690
What?

00:08:23.690 --> 00:08:25.310
In this soccer club,

00:08:25.310 --> 00:08:27.940
they don't allow any low chance 
plays like heel passes.

00:08:27.940 --> 00:08:30.130
Dribbles of longer than five 
seconds aren't allowed.

00:08:30.130 --> 00:08:32.270
It's a style of soccer that
 incorporates long balls,

00:08:32.270 --> 00:08:35.890
so players under 170cm 
aren't allowed to join.

00:08:35.890 --> 00:08:37.110
Seriously?

00:08:37.110 --> 00:08:40.060
Do you think it'd be 
any fun to play here?

00:08:40.060 --> 00:08:42.750
U-Um, Senpai, why do you...

00:08:43.610 --> 00:08:45.500
Get off your high horse!

00:08:46.300 --> 00:08:49.480
Is it any fun being a quitter?

00:08:49.480 --> 00:08:50.460
Mako-senpai!

00:08:50.460 --> 00:08:51.170
Huh?

00:08:53.890 --> 00:08:54.800
Watch out!

00:08:57.300 --> 00:08:57.890
What?

00:08:57.890 --> 00:08:59.100
Sea lion!

00:09:04.090 --> 00:09:05.590
Don't make me do that!

00:09:07.900 --> 00:09:08.760
It'll hit the glass!

00:09:15.860 --> 00:09:17.570
Nice header, Kinjiro.

00:09:17.800 --> 00:09:19.510
<i>Was that on purpose?</i>

00:09:19.510 --> 00:09:22.400
<i>If so, that was some 
amazing ball control.</i>

00:09:22.400 --> 00:09:24.540
<i>And the softness of that trap earlier...</i>

00:09:25.390 --> 00:09:26.790
<i>Who is this guy?</i>

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.790
Hi!

00:09:28.790 --> 00:09:30.270
I'm yellow card Mako!

00:09:30.270 --> 00:09:31.360
I'm Arackie!

00:09:31.360 --> 00:09:32.710
Together we're...

00:09:32.710 --> 00:09:33.760
Exiting!

00:09:33.760 --> 00:09:35.150
Exiting already?

00:09:35.150 --> 00:09:36.220
That was fast!

00:09:37.870 --> 00:09:41.080
Mako, focus on just the 
comedy club already.

00:09:41.080 --> 00:09:43.190
Let's aim to perform on a 
national level together.

00:09:43.190 --> 00:09:44.390
Yeah, well...

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:45.680
Um... Mako-senpai?

00:09:45.680 --> 00:09:47.420
Oh, let me introduce you.

00:09:47.420 --> 00:09:49.960
This guy is my partner in the 
comedy duo research club.

00:09:49.960 --> 00:09:51.790
He's Arackie, or Ryuichi Araki.

00:09:51.790 --> 00:09:52.400
Hi!

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.170
Arackie from the comedy club?

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:56.020
Ryuichi Araki-san...

00:09:56.910 --> 00:09:58.360
Ryuichi Araki?!

00:09:58.360 --> 00:09:59.200
What?

00:09:59.200 --> 00:10:03.410
Th-Then, the Araki-senpai 
that I've been looking for

00:10:04.260 --> 00:10:06.800
i-is him?!

00:10:08.370 --> 00:10:10.510
I guess. What's up, Aizawa-kun?

00:10:10.510 --> 00:10:12.590
Kakeru, keep it together!

00:10:12.950 --> 00:10:15.090
Kakeru... Aizawa?

00:10:15.090 --> 00:10:17.050
Suguru's brother?

00:10:17.050 --> 00:10:17.800
What?

00:10:21.120 --> 00:10:22.720
Hey, you guys!

00:10:23.280 --> 00:10:25.970
Don't get in the way 
of the soccer club.

00:10:25.970 --> 00:10:26.680
What?

00:10:27.420 --> 00:10:29.400
Um, Iwaki-sensei.

00:10:29.400 --> 00:10:31.150
What's going on?

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:34.610
Oh, I can see how this might 
be hard to understand.

00:10:34.940 --> 00:10:39.030
Actually, Enoshima High 
has two soccer teams.

00:10:39.570 --> 00:10:42.240
That's the school representative 
Enoshima High Soccer Club,

00:10:42.240 --> 00:10:43.890
also known as SC.

00:10:43.890 --> 00:10:48.320
We're the play-for-fun 
Enoshima High Football Club.

00:10:48.320 --> 00:10:50.390
So, we call ourselves FC.

00:10:50.390 --> 00:10:52.710
What? Play-for-fun?

00:10:52.710 --> 00:10:55.290
Yes, congratulations on getting in.

00:10:55.290 --> 00:10:56.420
I look forward to working together,

00:10:56.680 --> 00:10:58.630
Mishima-san, and Aizawa-kun.

00:10:59.470 --> 00:11:01.120
W-Wait a second!

00:11:01.120 --> 00:11:02.510
If this is just-for-fun, then I won't

00:11:02.510 --> 00:11:03.750
be able to compete in matches!

00:11:03.750 --> 00:11:05.070
Who cares?

00:11:05.070 --> 00:11:07.220
I'm in the comedy duo research club.

00:11:08.300 --> 00:11:12.180
I-I joined a play-for-fun club...

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:15.500
and the Araki-senpai my brother respected

00:11:15.500 --> 00:11:18.360
is a f-fat comedian...

00:11:18.560 --> 00:11:21.530
Ka-Kakeru!

00:11:23.610 --> 00:11:26.040
I-I'm sorry!

00:11:26.320 --> 00:11:29.320
I'd rather be in the official club!

00:11:29.320 --> 00:11:32.390
Please! Cancel my membership!

00:11:32.390 --> 00:11:35.310
Why do you want to be 
in the official club?

00:11:35.310 --> 00:11:38.210
B-Because, if I'm not 
in the official club,

00:11:38.210 --> 00:11:40.010
I can't compete in 
competitive matches, can I?

00:11:40.180 --> 00:11:41.780
Then I ask of you,

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:45.220
if you were to join the club, 
what are your goals?

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.630
Of course, I want to win regionals

00:11:47.630 --> 00:11:50.730
and to compete in, and win, nationals.

00:11:51.150 --> 00:11:52.420
I see...

00:11:54.660 --> 00:11:57.410
You're thinking you want to 
put up with the boring SC

00:11:57.410 --> 00:11:59.780
and play soccer because you're

00:11:59.780 --> 00:12:02.360
caught up in such small dreams.

00:12:02.920 --> 00:12:06.950
Nationals... winning nationals 
is a small dream?

00:12:06.950 --> 00:12:07.580
Right.

00:12:08.040 --> 00:12:11.990
Playing soccer aiming to win 
in such a small competition

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:14.040
is as small as Japan is to 
the rest of the world.

00:12:14.240 --> 00:12:16.160
In other countries,
 where soccer is popular,

00:12:16.160 --> 00:12:18.970
the dream that kids your age have

00:12:18.970 --> 00:12:20.760
is to play as a national representative

00:12:20.760 --> 00:12:23.220
and win the World Cup.

00:12:26.930 --> 00:12:29.210
We, the Enoshima High FC,

00:12:29.210 --> 00:12:32.020
play soccer on that 
sort of larger scale.

00:12:38.920 --> 00:12:39.980
Still,

00:12:39.980 --> 00:12:42.260
as a short term goal,
 winning regionals

00:12:42.260 --> 00:12:44.640
and national tournaments 
is important as well.

00:12:44.640 --> 00:12:47.210
Given the chance, this year

00:12:47.210 --> 00:12:49.700
I'd like to represent Enoshima High!

00:12:49.700 --> 00:12:50.700
Huh?

00:12:51.110 --> 00:12:55.420
Actually, before a large match, 
the SC and the FC face off

00:12:55.420 --> 00:12:58.420
to determine who will represent 
the school in the match.

00:12:58.420 --> 00:12:59.170
What?

00:12:59.190 --> 00:13:04.880
<b>Defeat SC!!</b>

00:12:59.410 --> 00:13:01.890
The winning team is the 
representative club

00:13:01.890 --> 00:13:04.020
and competes for the school.

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.210
How about it?

00:13:06.210 --> 00:13:09.050
For just a week, want to 
practice with everyone

00:13:09.050 --> 00:13:12.350
on the Enoshima High FC 
as a provisional player?

00:13:13.650 --> 00:13:14.570
<i>Brother...</i>

00:13:15.140 --> 00:13:18.520
Um... Is this the FC club room?

00:13:19.210 --> 00:13:19.970
Hello.

00:13:20.470 --> 00:13:22.860
<i>That's the kid who heel passed.</i>

00:13:23.140 --> 00:13:24.580
Yes, that's right.

00:13:24.870 --> 00:13:26.090
Are you interested in joining?

00:13:26.090 --> 00:13:29.910
Yes. I failed the SC test,

00:13:30.400 --> 00:13:32.870
but I want to play 
soccer no matter what!

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:33.860
So...

00:13:33.860 --> 00:13:36.050
Of course, you can join.

00:13:36.050 --> 00:13:38.040
Yes, yes, yes. What's your name?

00:13:38.040 --> 00:13:39.360
Matoba Kaoru.

00:13:39.360 --> 00:13:41.270
Kaoru, Kaoru-kun, right?

00:13:41.270 --> 00:13:42.930
I'm Mako. Let's get along!

00:13:42.930 --> 00:13:45.050
Nice to meet you all!

00:13:45.050 --> 00:13:46.980
Let's join here, Kakeru.

00:13:47.380 --> 00:13:48.130
Seven...

00:13:48.550 --> 00:13:49.970
It seems fun, right?

00:13:51.080 --> 00:13:51.740
Yeah.

00:13:53.060 --> 00:13:54.800
<i>My heart's stopped pounding.</i>

00:13:54.800 --> 00:13:56.390
<i>I guess my brother feels the same way.</i>

00:13:56.960 --> 00:14:00.010
Iwaki-sensei! 
I'd like to come to practices—

00:14:00.010 --> 00:14:02.650
I mean, please allow me to 
officially join your club!

00:14:02.650 --> 00:14:05.440
All right! We've made it to 11 members!

00:14:05.440 --> 00:14:06.860
We can actually play!

00:14:06.860 --> 00:14:09.250
What? You didn't have enough?

00:14:09.250 --> 00:14:10.220
Yeah...

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.760
But now, we can finally compete 
to represent the school.

00:14:13.760 --> 00:14:15.830
When is that match?

00:14:16.380 --> 00:14:17.700
In two weeks.

00:14:17.700 --> 00:14:18.540
What?!

00:14:19.030 --> 00:14:19.950
Well,

00:14:20.500 --> 00:14:23.170
don't get your hopes up.

00:14:24.060 --> 00:14:25.300
Araki-senpai!

00:14:25.930 --> 00:14:29.430
Let me just say that the SC's 
strength is the real thing.

00:14:30.000 --> 00:14:32.550
It's not the kind of club that 
a play-for-fun club can beat.

00:14:34.270 --> 00:14:35.270
Kakeru!

00:14:40.330 --> 00:14:41.340
Araki-san...

00:14:57.960 --> 00:14:59.140
Araki-senpai—

00:15:06.170 --> 00:15:07.300
Araki-senpai.

00:15:07.930 --> 00:15:11.410
You used to play soccer 
for the FC, didn't you?

00:15:11.410 --> 00:15:13.350
What about it?

00:15:21.620 --> 00:15:23.160
Won't you try again?

00:15:23.720 --> 00:15:27.310
I want to try to receive 
your pass! So...

00:15:27.310 --> 00:15:29.620
Did your dead brother 
tell you something?

00:15:29.620 --> 00:15:31.320
You're Suguru's brother, right?

00:15:31.320 --> 00:15:33.320
It was in my brother's diary.

00:15:33.320 --> 00:15:36.290
He said you had better 
pass intuition than him.

00:15:36.590 --> 00:15:37.490
Cut it out!

00:15:38.930 --> 00:15:41.900
He despised me.

00:15:41.900 --> 00:15:45.140
Called me a spineless, 
selfish, naked king.

00:15:45.140 --> 00:15:46.380
B-But...

00:15:46.860 --> 00:15:50.800
The main reason I thought 
about quitting soccer

00:15:50.800 --> 00:15:52.090
was your brother.

00:15:55.780 --> 00:15:56.930
<b>Enoshima High FC</b>

00:15:56.400 --> 00:15:59.020
Let's go to practice!

00:15:59.320 --> 00:16:00.840
Put these on, freshmen!

00:16:04.760 --> 00:16:09.850
One, two, three, four, 
five, six, seven, eight.

00:16:10.770 --> 00:16:12.910
How did this happen?

00:16:13.730 --> 00:16:15.550
Sorry to keep you waiting!

00:16:18.920 --> 00:16:20.810
Definitely a mascot girl.

00:16:20.810 --> 00:16:22.280
Perfect size...

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:26.670
Bring it in!

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.770
As always,

00:16:28.770 --> 00:16:32.160
let's start with some 
beach soccer scrimmage.

00:16:32.160 --> 00:16:34.470
Break up into two teams of five.

00:16:34.470 --> 00:16:35.140
Okay!

00:16:35.510 --> 00:16:37.050
Beach soccer?

00:16:37.050 --> 00:16:38.950
Unlike the official SC,

00:16:38.950 --> 00:16:40.940
we can't use most of the school grounds.

00:16:40.940 --> 00:16:43.350
Our beach soccer rules are 
a little different as well.

00:16:43.500 --> 00:16:44.790
There's only one goal.

00:16:44.790 --> 00:16:46.660
It's between those two flags.

00:16:46.660 --> 00:16:48.920
If a defender steals the ball and 
kicks it into the ocean,

00:16:48.920 --> 00:16:50.570
you switch sides and restart the game.

00:16:50.990 --> 00:16:52.860
White team kick off!

00:16:53.970 --> 00:16:54.670
Okay!

00:16:59.300 --> 00:17:01.330
<i>A bold, quick slide!</i>

00:17:01.330 --> 00:17:04.280
<i>I see, the reason Coach
 Iwaki chose to practice</i>

00:17:04.280 --> 00:17:06.220
<i>on the beach was to...</i>

00:17:06.220 --> 00:17:06.830
Shoot!

00:17:07.300 --> 00:17:08.810
<i>It's so hard to run!</i>

00:17:08.810 --> 00:17:09.550
Aizawa!

00:17:12.420 --> 00:17:13.240
I'll take that!

00:17:13.240 --> 00:17:14.010
Shit!

00:17:14.010 --> 00:17:16.580
The sands keeps the ball 
from moving at all!

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:17.840
That's why this is great practice

00:17:17.840 --> 00:17:19.300
to improve quick and strong passes!

00:17:20.510 --> 00:17:21.520
Here I go!

00:17:23.320 --> 00:17:24.570
Nice pass, Mako!

00:17:24.570 --> 00:17:25.740
Okay, change-up.

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:26.810
Shit!

00:17:28.320 --> 00:17:30.480
Hey, newcomer.

00:17:30.480 --> 00:17:32.490
Are you going to be okay 
going all out like that?

00:17:32.490 --> 00:17:33.820
Freshman!

00:17:35.320 --> 00:17:38.010
That pass would be impossible 
for that newcomer.

00:17:38.660 --> 00:17:39.700
I'll be taking—

00:17:39.700 --> 00:17:40.490
What?

00:17:40.680 --> 00:17:41.950
It's not over yet!

00:17:42.240 --> 00:17:44.200
<i>He's already caught up?</i>

00:17:44.200 --> 00:17:45.690
<i>Did he predict where the ball</i>

00:17:45.690 --> 00:17:47.730
<i>would go and run straight over?</i>

00:17:47.730 --> 00:17:48.900
Got it!

00:17:57.650 --> 00:18:00.590
<i>Amazing! Mako-san and Kurebayashi-san.</i>

00:18:00.590 --> 00:18:03.750
<i>I've never seen a team 
use such bold moves.</i>

00:18:03.750 --> 00:18:07.390
<i>Brother, this team's 
soccer is so much fun!</i>

00:18:09.760 --> 00:18:12.400
That's the first half. It's halftime.

00:18:16.960 --> 00:18:18.660
Are you alive, Kakeru?

00:18:18.660 --> 00:18:20.690
B-Barely.

00:18:20.690 --> 00:18:23.660
But your leg muscles are twitching...

00:18:23.660 --> 00:18:24.860
Hey! Hey!

00:18:24.860 --> 00:18:26.330
Hey, cut it out, Seven.

00:18:26.330 --> 00:18:28.790
What are you looking at?

00:18:30.080 --> 00:18:32.500
That female manager's swimsuit...

00:18:32.770 --> 00:18:34.960
That Aizawa's caught your eye, hasn't he?

00:18:35.400 --> 00:18:37.870
He's Suguru Aizawa's brother, right?

00:18:37.870 --> 00:18:38.720
That's why you...

00:18:38.720 --> 00:18:39.430
Irrelevant.

00:18:39.680 --> 00:18:40.980
I wonder about that.

00:18:40.980 --> 00:18:42.500
So, what do you think?

00:18:42.500 --> 00:18:44.280
In your eyes, he's...

00:18:44.280 --> 00:18:46.100
Middle school level.

00:18:46.100 --> 00:18:48.890
As it is, he can't 
compete in high school.

00:18:49.100 --> 00:18:50.490
So strict.

00:18:50.870 --> 00:18:52.720
I think he's got potential.

00:18:52.720 --> 00:18:54.710
He's got a troubling weakness.

00:18:54.710 --> 00:18:55.360
Weakness?

00:18:56.140 --> 00:18:59.070
But his intuition in the 
penalty area is valuable.

00:18:59.430 --> 00:19:01.370
That's not something you 
gain through practice.

00:19:01.370 --> 00:19:02.280
He's a genius.

00:19:02.840 --> 00:19:04.830
An incomplete genius.

00:19:04.830 --> 00:19:05.860
Same as you, then...

00:19:05.860 --> 00:19:06.970
Shut it.

00:19:08.490 --> 00:19:09.460
Hey, Araki.

00:19:10.100 --> 00:19:12.240
Everyone wants you to come back.

00:19:12.830 --> 00:19:15.720
Aizawa, you, me, and everyone else...

00:19:15.720 --> 00:19:17.670
Sure, each of us is incomplete.

00:19:17.670 --> 00:19:20.750
But as a team, being able to 
cover for each other's weakness

00:19:20.750 --> 00:19:21.890
is what soccer's all about.

00:19:22.100 --> 00:19:25.710
I already quit.
I don't intend to come back.

00:19:25.710 --> 00:19:27.130
Araki!

00:19:27.130 --> 00:19:28.870
What are you saying?

00:19:28.870 --> 00:19:32.470
Then why are you always 
wearing soccer shoes?

00:19:32.470 --> 00:19:34.600
When I first met you,

00:19:34.600 --> 00:19:37.080
you said you always wore soccer 
shoes to break them in.

00:19:37.080 --> 00:19:39.430
You said that, for a match, 
you'd change the studs.

00:19:39.430 --> 00:19:41.970
You wear soccer shoes all the time?

00:19:41.970 --> 00:19:44.600
I always wear them to break them in

00:19:44.600 --> 00:19:46.790
and I just change the 
studs for matches.

00:19:49.130 --> 00:19:51.830
<i>A guy who says the same 
thing as you has joined.</i>

00:19:52.280 --> 00:19:55.990
<i>Come back, Ryuichi Araki.</i>

00:19:58.340 --> 00:19:59.270
I'm home!

00:20:00.500 --> 00:20:03.400
<i>That my brother could 
despise Araki-san...</i>

00:20:04.910 --> 00:20:07.830
He's a naked king...

00:20:05.540 --> 00:20:06.530
This is...

00:20:09.070 --> 00:20:09.850
Play-for-fun club?

00:20:10.110 --> 00:20:13.610
Yeah, I was recruited by 
this interesting guy, Iwaki.

00:20:13.610 --> 00:20:15.560
We're still looking for players, though.

00:20:15.910 --> 00:20:17.500
Are you underestimating soccer?

00:20:17.500 --> 00:20:18.240
What?

00:20:18.240 --> 00:20:20.430
What will you get playing 
like a king for a team

00:20:20.430 --> 00:20:21.780
that won't even let you 
play in a real match?

00:20:22.040 --> 00:20:23.240
Shut up!

00:20:24.170 --> 00:20:25.700
<i>I was genuinely disappointed.</i>

00:20:26.170 --> 00:20:27.370
<i>If I'd known this would happen,</i>

00:20:27.280 --> 00:20:31.660
He's a naked king...

00:20:27.370 --> 00:20:28.690
<i>I wish I hadn't met him.</i>

00:20:29.230 --> 00:20:31.370
<i>He's a naked king.</i>

00:20:32.370 --> 00:20:33.430
<i>He misunderstood.</i>

00:20:33.430 --> 00:20:37.170
<i>Araki-senpai chose to join 
the play-for-fun FC team</i>

00:20:37.170 --> 00:20:38.800
<i>not because he was being selfish,</i>

00:20:39.670 --> 00:20:42.130
<i>but because he believed he could</i>

00:20:42.130 --> 00:20:43.720
<i>play his own soccer with that team!</i>

00:20:48.910 --> 00:20:52.830
The main reason I thought 
about quitting soccer

00:20:52.830 --> 00:20:54.440
was your brother.

00:20:55.110 --> 00:20:56.540
<i>That's wrong!</i>

00:20:56.890 --> 00:20:57.920
<i>Wrong!</i>

00:20:59.440 --> 00:21:02.490
By the way, Kota-kun, 
how did the SC test go?

00:21:02.490 --> 00:21:04.390
I barely passed, somehow,

00:21:04.390 --> 00:21:06.320
but then I panicked when 
I saw them practice.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:08.430
They have an unbelievable team.

00:21:08.910 --> 00:21:10.120
Excuse me.

00:21:10.840 --> 00:21:11.830
Oda-san!

00:21:12.810 --> 00:21:14.560
The practice match has been decided.

00:21:14.970 --> 00:21:17.080
I don't think you'll play,
but after school,

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:21.030
be sure to meet on the grounds 
wearing your uniform.

00:21:21.030 --> 00:21:22.260
Understood!

00:21:22.260 --> 00:21:22.980
That's all.

00:21:26.300 --> 00:21:27.510
You're Aizawa-kun, right?

00:21:27.510 --> 00:21:28.870
Y-Yes!

00:21:29.220 --> 00:21:32.190
If you'd like, come watch 
our practice match.

00:21:32.610 --> 00:21:33.560
Okay...

00:21:36.620 --> 00:21:38.560
Kakeru, that guy...

00:21:38.560 --> 00:21:40.750
A second year, Ryoma Oda-san.

00:21:40.750 --> 00:21:43.590
He's the one wearing number 10 for SC.

00:21:43.590 --> 00:21:44.770
<i>This match...</i>

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:52.030
<b>Enoshima 0     Kaihin 0
Team   First Half   Second Half   Total</b>

00:21:50.010 --> 00:21:52.040
Twenty minutes into the first half.

00:21:52.360 --> 00:21:54.530
They're evenly matched, so far.

00:21:54.530 --> 00:21:56.870
Is that how it looks to 
the brother of a genius?

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:58.330
Araki-senpai!

00:21:59.060 --> 00:22:00.810
So, you're concerned 
about the representative

00:22:00.810 --> 00:22:02.080
deciding match as well?

00:22:02.080 --> 00:22:04.300
You shouldn't be so 
stubborn. Come back.

00:22:04.760 --> 00:22:07.460
You want me to play beach 
soccer for three years,

00:22:07.460 --> 00:22:09.260
with a team that can't even 
compete in matches?

00:22:09.590 --> 00:22:11.220
We don't know yet.

00:22:11.620 --> 00:22:12.990
I know.

00:22:12.990 --> 00:22:16.440
At the match last year, 
it was etched deeply in my mind.

00:22:17.300 --> 00:22:18.940
What kind of match was it?

00:22:19.740 --> 00:22:21.900
Just like this one.

00:22:22.260 --> 00:22:23.630
So high!

00:22:24.080 --> 00:22:25.130
Stop him!

00:22:25.130 --> 00:22:26.050
Takase!

00:22:30.050 --> 00:22:33.350
The SC's strategy is always the same.

00:22:33.350 --> 00:22:35.820
It's simple but, when mastered, effective.

00:22:35.820 --> 00:22:38.780
The one who scored was the 
newcomer, Michiro Takase.

00:22:38.780 --> 00:22:40.750
He's 190cm tall.

00:22:40.750 --> 00:22:42.670
<b>Enoshima 1     Kaihin 0
Team   First Half   Second Half   Total</b>

00:22:41.340 --> 00:22:42.670
First half is over!

00:22:43.190 --> 00:22:44.740
In other words, SC's soccer

00:22:44.740 --> 00:22:46.040
involves using physically strong players

00:22:46.040 --> 00:22:48.050
to their maximum potential.

00:22:48.600 --> 00:22:51.620
How advantageous are the 
weapons they were born with.

00:22:51.620 --> 00:22:54.430
But they never tire of 
their monotonous strategy.

00:22:54.430 --> 00:22:55.470
In comparison,

00:22:55.470 --> 00:22:57.730
we, who had tried to attack 
with detailed techniques,

00:22:57.730 --> 00:23:00.150
used up our endurance until 
were completely exhausted.

00:23:00.770 --> 00:23:03.100
Just like the Kaihin team now.

00:23:03.790 --> 00:23:05.880
The second half was even more tragic.

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:07.820
They covered us completely,

00:23:07.820 --> 00:23:10.280
and when we panicked and 
let our guard down,

00:23:10.280 --> 00:23:12.250
they'd counter with another point.

00:23:12.250 --> 00:23:15.790
We were caught in a vicious 
cycle, just like Kaihin is now.

00:23:17.130 --> 00:23:21.740
In soccer, defense is the best offense.

00:23:22.750 --> 00:23:25.630
5-0. Enoshima wins.

00:23:25.950 --> 00:23:28.530
We lost 4-1.

00:23:28.530 --> 00:23:30.950
Just as Suguru had said.

00:23:31.480 --> 00:23:33.230
Who scored that point?

00:23:33.230 --> 00:23:33.850
Huh?

00:23:33.850 --> 00:23:35.740
It was 4-1, right?

00:23:35.740 --> 00:23:37.810
Who scored that one point?

00:23:38.080 --> 00:23:39.520
The middle, me.

00:23:39.520 --> 00:23:41.980
Just before the match 
ended, I put it in.

00:23:41.980 --> 00:23:44.270
You hadn't given up then, at that time.

00:23:44.270 --> 00:23:45.990
Up until the end of the game,

00:23:45.990 --> 00:23:47.600
weren't you trying to score?

00:23:47.600 --> 00:23:48.310
Then why would yo—

00:23:48.310 --> 00:23:50.240
You don't know what 
you're talking about!

00:23:50.580 --> 00:23:52.310
No matter how hard I looked,

00:23:52.310 --> 00:23:56.450
I couldn't find a pass route 
through their defense.

00:23:56.790 --> 00:23:58.700
If you can't find one, make one.

00:23:58.700 --> 00:23:59.660
What?

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:01.970
Let's make it together.

00:24:01.970 --> 00:24:04.230
A pass route that will bring down

00:24:04.230 --> 00:24:05.630
their iron defense in an instant.

00:24:07.250 --> 00:24:09.030
It's not often that I get

00:24:09.030 --> 00:24:11.550
a pass route that feels so great.

00:24:11.550 --> 00:24:14.360
Yeah. You're something, all right,

00:24:14.360 --> 00:24:17.030
but I know of an even better pass.

00:24:17.030 --> 00:24:17.560
Huh?

00:24:17.850 --> 00:24:19.600
A pass that you don't find by yourself,

00:24:19.600 --> 00:24:21.030
but you make with someone else.

00:24:23.730 --> 00:24:25.030
I'm serious!

00:24:25.030 --> 00:24:26.860
I'm seriously aiming to win 
the national tournament!

00:24:26.860 --> 00:24:27.980
So, Araki-san!

00:24:28.570 --> 00:24:31.300
It's okay. You got through to him.

00:24:31.710 --> 00:24:32.950
Your feelings got through.

00:24:33.540 --> 00:24:36.220
Now it just depends on 
him, don't you think?

00:24:36.220 --> 00:24:37.010
Yeah.

00:24:39.120 --> 00:24:45.710
<b>2 weeks later</b>

00:24:39.970 --> 00:24:43.350
<i>Finally, the day of the 
decisive match arrived.</i>

00:24:45.980 --> 00:25:15.430
<b>Next Episode: 
Clash! FC vs SC!!</b>

00:24:47.020 --> 00:24:50.700
Finally, the decisive match against 
the rival team, SC, begins.

00:24:50.700 --> 00:24:52.680
Against the SC's perfect soccer,

00:24:52.680 --> 00:24:55.390
the FC resolutely challenges 
with unrestrained expression.

00:24:55.390 --> 00:24:57.720
But, unable to obtain 
a decisive feeling,

00:24:57.720 --> 00:25:00.340
the FC is faced with a vast 
difference in strength.

00:25:00.340 --> 00:25:02.050
However, continuing to fight 
and believing in victory,

00:25:02.050 --> 00:25:04.320
Kakeru and the others, twenty 
 minutes into the second half,

00:25:04.320 --> 00:25:06.310
are faced with the biggest crisis.

00:25:06.310 --> 00:25:08.230
What will you do, Kakeru?

00:25:08.230 --> 00:25:09.850
Next time on 
The Knight in the Area:

00:25:09.850 --> 00:25:13.500
the sixth episode,
 "Clash! FC vs SC!!"

00:25:13.500 --> 00:25:14.990
Finish it, Kakeru!
